        "verse": 29
      },
      "raw_locator": [
        {
          "book": "ISA",
          "chapter": 37,
          "verse": 29
        }
      ],
      "en": "Because of your raging against me, and because your arrogance has come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your nose and my bridle in your lips, and I will turn you back by the way by which you came.",
      "ko": "네가 나를 거스려 분노함과 네 오만함이 내 귀에 들렸으므로 내가 갈고리로 네 코를 꿰며 자갈을 네 입에 먹여 너를 오던 길로 돌아가게 하리라 하셨나이다",
      "source_text_hash": "002a68d9afd2504a51664150817e7cb24b5e5440d1e945061f9ec555b551e254",
      "translation_text_hash": "f5b820c6a4d1c33449c4ce797de22ed22e6cf2b366ce34834ec8b8241370e98c",
      "translation_policy": "krv-1961-source-mapped",
      "source_edition": "KRV-1961",
      "mapping_type": "normal",
      "mapping_note": null,
      "raw_texts": [
